import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout title="About Hydraulic Toolbox" description="Why Hydraulic Toolbox exists and how its calculators and field references are designed.">
  <section class="page-hero"><div class="container"><span class="eyebrow">About</span><h1 style="font-size:clamp(2.4rem,6vw,4.7rem);margin-top:12px">Built around real workshop questions</h1><p class="lead">Hydraulic Toolbox is a focused technical utility site: short paths to calculations, measurements and diagnostic clues instead of generic articles written only to attract clicks.</p></div></section>
  <section class="section compact"><div class="container article"><h2>Editorial principle</h2><p>Every page should answer a practical question, show its assumptions and make it easier for the user to verify the result. Calculators expose formulas; reference pages focus on measurable dimensions; guides are structured around field workflows.</p><h2>What comes next</h2><p>The first growth loop is simple: publish high-value tools, watch real search queries, improve pages that earn impressions, then expand into adjacent calculators and references. Monetization is layered on top rather than driving the content itself.</p></div></section>
</BaseLayout>
